#: source/installation/single-user.md:1
msgid "Single-User Mode"
msgstr "單使用者模式"

#: source/installation/single-user.md:3
msgid ""
"In single-user mode, all Nix operations that access the database in `prefix/"
"var/nix/db` or modify the Nix store in `prefix/store` must be performed "
"under the user ID that owns those directories. This is typically root. (If "
"you install from RPM packages, that’s in fact the default ownership.) "
"However, on single-user machines, it is often convenient to `chown` those "
"directories to your normal user account so that you don’t have to `su` to "
"root all the time."
msgstr ""
